    },
    {
      "id": "fS7KMrKdtKsI6pcEKgL6S",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -396.40810412930665,
      "y": 4725.863771483006,
      "width": 900.1390991210938,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#12b886",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aKS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 658841327,
      "version": 1266,
      "versionNonce": 246574273,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "mthwqWIsIIZJKaiExezna",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1776810859804,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Components (Microservices/Modules) communicate with each other in two ways,\nfor synchronous operations that require immediate response, the component calls \nthe other component's internal REST API endpoints.\n\nFor operations that could take a long time to finish (or at all), asynchronous communication\nis used in the form of publishing/subscribing to message queue.  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Components (Microservices/Modules) communicate with each other in two ways,\nfor synchronous operations that require immediate response, the component calls \nthe other component's internal REST API endpoints.\n\nFor operations that could take a long time to finish (or at all), asynchronous communication\nis used in the form of publishing/subscribing to message queue.  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "mjAP-B_QwmEKmMUD3LRpp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 768.4223467881545,
      "y": 4693.477494373671,
      "width": 900.1390991210938,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#12b886",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aKU",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1464101729,
      "version": 1329,
      "versionNonce": 857818689,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776858127483,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Components (Microservices/Modules) communicate with each other in two ways,\nfor synchronous operations that require immediate response, the component calls \nthe other component's internal REST API endpoints.\n\nFor operations that could take a long time to finish (or at all), asynchronous communication\nis used in the form of publishing/subscribing to message queue.  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Components (Microservices/Modules) communicate with each other in two ways,\nfor synchronous operations that require immediate response, the component calls \nthe other component's internal REST API endpoints.\n\nFor operations that could take a long time to finish (or at all), asynchronous communication\nis used in the form of publishing/subscribing to message queue.  ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ktXNQrMLuVdkdC5q2wtAc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 92.30401422064222,
      "y": 3061.331250194633,
      "width": 1078.618896484375,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#12b886",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aKV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 436314912,
      "version": 2467,
      "versionNonce": 1306986553,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776772108024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Capybara cloud exposes two main types of interface, HTTP REST API server admin and client apps,\nand an MCP Service interfaces for AI models to communicate with.  \n\n\nThe nature of a our service (Platform) requires that applications can be deployed to multiple servers,\nideally at multiple different locations for reliability and scalability, and it that it must be resillient.\n\nA failure in deployment module, shouldnt make already deployed applications to be suddenly unreachable,\nlikewise, if we run out of host resources, we may want to still be able to accept deployment requests,\nand process them later after the new resource have been made available (e.g by upgrading the hosts, \nadding more hosts). \n\n\nThe deployment and provisioning modules are strong candidate to be deployed independently of other modules,\ntherefore we will develop them as microservices from the beginning.\n\nThe space management functionalities are mostly basic CRUD operations, and their scope are small enough\nthat we can keep them in a single microservice.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Capybara cloud exposes two main types of interface, HTTP REST API server admin and client apps,\nand an MCP Service interfaces for AI models to communicate with.  \n\n\nThe nature of a our service (Platform) requires that applications can be deployed to multiple servers,\nideally at multiple different locations for reliability and scalability, and it that it must be resillient.\n\nA failure in deployment module, shouldnt make already deployed applications to be suddenly unreachable,\nlikewise, if we run out of host resources, we may want to still be able to accept deployment requests,\nand process them later after the new resource have been made available (e.g by upgrading the hosts, \nadding more hosts). \n\n\nThe deployment and provisioning modules are strong candidate to be deployed independently of other modules,\ntherefore we will develop them as microservices from the beginning.\n\nThe space management functionalities are mostly basic CRUD operations, and their scope are small enough\nthat we can keep them in a single microservice.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
