      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The provisioning service tracks the state of the hosts, The service keeps an in-memory\ncopy of a subset of registered hosts from the database.\n\nThe goal of copying this data is so the service can derive a data structure to make\ndeciding which host to run the applications on efficiently while the best utilization of \nall registered hosts.\n\nThe goal of copying this data is so the service can derive a data structure to make\ndeciding which host to run the applications on efficiently while the best utilization of \nall registered hosts. \n\nFor starter, this data structure can be a simple list, to get the next host on top of which\nto run the app, find the first matching item (host having enough resource), \nsend a message for it to pull metadata from the space module, pull the source code, build, and run.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The provisioning service tracks the state of the hosts, The service keeps an in-memory\ncopy of a subset of registered hosts from the database.\n\nThe goal of copying this data is so the service can derive a data structure to make\ndeciding which host to run the applications on efficiently while the best utilization of \nall registered hosts.\n\nThe goal of copying this data is so the service can derive a data structure to make\ndeciding which host to run the applications on efficiently while the best utilization of \nall registered hosts. \n\nFor starter, this data structure can be a simple list, to get the next host on top of which\nto run the app, find the first matching item (host having enough resource), \nsend a message for it to pull metadata from the space module, pull the source code, build, and run.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
